@startuml
title Customer order delivery - high level view

participant "ProductOrderCaptureValidation" as POCV
participant "ProductOrderOrchestrationManagement" as POOM
participant "ProductCatalogManagement" as PCM
participant "EventManagement" as Event
participant "ProductInventory" as PI

== Order Delivery step 1 ==

POCV -> Event : 1 **TMF688 Event Management** POST /productOrderStateChangeEvent\n(state="accepted")
Event --> POOM : 2 **TMF688 Event Management** POST listener/productOrderStateChangeEvent\n(state="accepted")
activate POOM

POOM -> POOM : 3 **TMF701 Process Flow** POST /processFlow\n(ProcessFlowSpec=POOM + ProductOrderId1)

POOM -> POCV : 4 **TMF622 Product Ordering** GET /productOrder/id1
activate POCV
POCV --> POOM : 5 **TMF622** 200 OK\n(ProductOrder representation)
deactivate POCV

note right of POOM : PrdOrdOrcMgmt manages only ProductSpec level order item delivery

POOM -> POOM : 6 initiate delivery graph

loop compute PrdOrdCptVd delivery flow till item to be delivered
    POOM -> POOM : 7 Identify productSpec(s) to be managed

    alt Retrieve catalog information for product to be fullfilled
        note right of POOM
          catalog information distribution to POOM could be discussed
          as several options possibles (API access, Batch copy, etc.)
        end note
        POOM -> PCM : 8 **TMF620 Product Catalog Management** GET /productSpecification/id1
        activate PCM
        PCM --> POOM : 9 **TMF620** 200 OK\n(ProductSpecification information : support CFS / Stock Item)
        deactivate PCM
    end

    note right of POOM : UC did not feature existing assets modification - Inventory API not used

    group Manage delivery depending on type of productSpec
        note right of POOM
          Flow for the UC to be describe
           - for service based see CFS-Based delivery
           - for goods see stock based delivery
        end note
    end

    POOM -> POOM : 10 update delivery graph
end

note right of POOM : Flow for order follow up is described in another diagram
deactivate POOM

@enduml
